<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Léon Humblot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1852–1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Léon Humblot was a French naturalist and adventurer who went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a> in 1884 to collect plants. He backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-ali-bin-said-omar">Said Ali of Bambao</a> as sultan of the whole island, and in 1886 obtained both a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and a concession over much of the island's land. He served for years as French resident and ran large plantations of vanilla and other crops.</p></div>
